# Landing Page SEO

When modifying any landing-page file, check and maintain the following:

## Metadata
- `app/layout.tsx` has global OG + Twitter metadata. Keep descriptions aligned with actual page content.
- `app/page.tsx` has page-level title, description, and `alternates.canonical`. Update if the hero tagline or core messaging changes.
- `app/opengraph-image.tsx` dynamically generates the OG image using the icon from `public/icons/icon-512x512.png`. Update tagline/subtitle there if it changes on the page.

## Structured Data (JSON-LD)
- `components/landing/landing-json-ld.tsx` renders three schemas: `WebSite`, `SoftwareApplication`, `FAQPage`.
- When FAQ items change in `messages/landing/en.json` → `faq.items`, the FAQ schema updates automatically via i18n.
- When pricing changes → update the `offers` array in `landing-json-ld.tsx`.

## Heading Hierarchy
- Exactly one `<h1>` on the landing page (in `hero-section.tsx`).
- Each section uses `<h2>`, sub-items use `<h3>`. Do not skip levels.

## Images
- Every `<img>` must have a descriptive `alt` attribute (not just "logo").

## Sitemap & Robots
- `app/sitemap.ts` — add entries when new public pages are created.
- `app/robots.ts` — keep `/app/`, `/api/`, `/auth/` disallowed.

## i18n
- Keep `messages/landing/en.json` and `de.json` in sync for any user-visible text changes.
